            <ArticleTitle>High spinal block following an inadequate continuous spinal anaesthetic.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>530-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A patient is presented who obtained only an L1 sensory block, which was inadequate for her procedure, from continuous spinal anaesthesia despite appropriate doses of 0.5% plain bupivacaine. She then developed a high spinal block after an epidural was sited and a test dose given in the sitting position. The possible mechanisms for this are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
